        },
        "texto": "The margin has “upper lip,” that is, the lip-beard or mustache, as the word sapham is rendered by Gesenius and others. The Hebrews held the beard in high estimation as a mark of manliness. To cover the lip, and thus conceal the beard growing there, was a sign of sorrow or of mour…"
      }
